## Rotating Card – CSS Only

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card with a front and a back side.  
When you hover over the card it flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (the element that flips) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s;    /* smooth animation */
}

/* Hover triggers the flip */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front face */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4e54c8, #8f94fb);
}

/* Back face – rotate 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff416c, #ff4b2b);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      <p>Front Side</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      <p>Back Side</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | CSS property |
|------|--------------|--------------|
| 1 | The wrapper gives the 3D space (`perspective`) | `perspective: 1000px;` |
| 2 | The `.card` holds both faces and keeps them in 3D (`transform-style: preserve-3d`) | `transform-style: preserve-3d;` |
| 3 | Each face is absolutely positioned and hidden when facing away (`backface-visibility: hidden`) | `backface-visibility: hidden;` |
| 4 | On hover the card is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |
| 5 | The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it becomes visible after the flip | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |

Feel free to replace the gradients, text, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a vertical flip instead, change `rotateY` to `rotateX`.
